WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.637
A default parameter gives the function a value to use when the caller does not provide one.

00:00:05.637 --> 00:00:08.977
Here the default tax rate is ten percent.

00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:15.177
Calling calculate_tax with only five hundred uses that rate and returns fifty.

00:00:15.177 --> 00:00:23.131
If we supply zero point one five as a second argument, the default is overridden and the tax becomes seventy-five.

00:00:23.747 --> 00:00:30.469
Defaults are useful for common assumptions, but they should be chosen carefully and documented clearly so the caller

00:00:30.469 --> 00:00:32.591
knows what will happen.
